      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code and won't start. i looked at the manual but it's kind of confusing. can u tell me how to check the leak sensor and how to actually dry out the base of the machine properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An E15 error code generally indicates a water level problem. Start by checking for leaks in the dishwasher, particularly around the door, hoses, and pump. Ensure that the low water level switch is working correctly by carefully inspecting and cleaning it, if necessary. To dry out the base, clean any debris around the bottom and bottom rack, then turn off the machine and plug it out for a few minutes until any residual water evaporates. Restart your dishwasher to see if the issue resolves. If the problem persists, it may require professional assistance.",
